EXT. WATER TOWER - STALLED TRAIN - HIGH DESERT - DAY

A locomotive idles at a sun-blasted siding. The wooden tank towers above, dripping from its spout. Dust. A coil of rope. A line of boxcars stretching behind into the heat.

ENGINEER SILAS DUNBAR (50s, striped cap, grease to the elbows) hangs from the water spout, wrestling the chain. Below him, FIREMAN CALLUM NAKAGAWA (20s, bare-chested, black with soot) braces the ladder. Standing in the shade of the tank, hand on her pistol, waits MARSHAL DELPHINE ARCENEAUX (40s, tan duster, silver badge).

A telegraph key chatters from the little station beside the track. Up on the first boxcar roof, CONDUCTOR BARTHOLOMEW ENGSTROM (60s, brass buttons, pocket watch) cups his hands to his mouth.

BARTHOLOMEW
Passengers inside! Shutters down!

TELEGRAPH CLERK (O.S.)
(shouting from the station)
Marshal! Wire from Santa Fe! Riders on the ridge!

DELPHINE
How many?

TELEGRAPH CLERK (O.S.)
Eight! Maybe ten!

SILAS
(from the spout)
Callum, haul!

CALLUM
Hauling!

DELPHINE
Silas, how long for the tank?

SILAS
Five minutes!

DELPHINE
You have two.

Callum strains on the chain. The spout swings; water crashes down in a silver wall, drenching the three of them as they grab the ladder, the pipe, the pistol, and scatter in separate directions. Silas drops to the ties. Callum leaps for the cab. Delphine drops to one knee and raises her rifle toward the ridge.

On the ridge, tiny horsemen appear against the sky.

DELPHINE (CONT'D)
Callum! Full steam!

CALLUM
Aye!

The locomotive shrieks. Steam bursts. The train lurches forward.
